    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] \"Krylya\") is a 1966 Soviet black and white drama film directed by Ukrainian filmmaker Larisa Shepitko, her first feature film made after graduating from the All-Russian State Institute for Cinematography.\n[2] Larisa Efimovna Shepitko (Russian: Лари́са Ефи́мовна Шепи́тько ; Ukrainian: Лариса Юхимівна Шепітько ; 6 January 1938 – 2 July 1979) was a Soviet film director, screenwriter and actress.\n[3] Klimov is best known in the West for his final film, 1985's \"Come and See\" (\"Иди и смотри\"), which follows a teenage boy in German-occupied Belarus during the German-Soviet War and is often considered one of the greatest war films ever made.\n[4] Joshua Dugdale, FRSA (Birmingham 1974), is a British documentary film-maker."
